<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Width of the in-app status panel.

      The panel mirrors the home-screen widget, whose provider declares a **4x2**
      footprint (see xml/widget_anc_info.xml — `targetCellWidth=4`,
      `targetCellHeight=2`). This comment said 3x2 for a long time after the widget
      was widened, as did README.md; the file itself is the authority. On a phone,
      letting that design run to match_parent stretched the battery bars across the
      whole screen and looked wrong, so the panel is capped to something close to
      the widget's own proportions and the remaining width is left free on the right.

      200dp is deliberately a hair narrower than the widget's own width so it reads
      as a compact card rather than a full-width bar. Raise this one value to widen
      the panel; nothing else needs changing.

      NOTE: this comment previously cited `activity_status_panel.xml` as the panel's
      layout. That file no longer exists — the main screen is `activity_main.xml` and
      the panel is built inside it (`batteryCard` / `batteryBarsCard`). Kept as a
      warning: a reference to a deleted layout is the kind of stale detail that sends
      the next session looking for a file that is not there.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_panel_width">200dp</dimen>

    <!--
      Height of the in-app status panel.

      The panel is a 3-row stack (battery card : ANC switcher : game row, weights
      3:1:1). Previously its parent gave it match_parent height, so it stretched to
      the bottom of the screen — which left a large dead area beside it AND left no
      room for the feature list below. It is now capped to a compact, roughly 2x2
      card shape, and the space underneath is reserved for the feature rows
      (dual device, spatial audio, codec, EQ, find my earbuds).

      148dp is sized to fit the three rows at their natural weights with the 88dp
      bud column still readable. Raise it if the rows look cramped; the weights
      re-distribute automatically.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_panel_height">148dp</dimen>

    <!-- Header icon button size (settings cog / dev tools). -->
    <dimen name="header_icon_button">36dp</dimen>

    <!-- Header title size, matched to the widget's primary label weight. -->
    <dimen name="header_title_size">16sp</dimen>

    <!-- ==================== Redesigned home screen ==================== -->

    <!--
      Battery card. Mirrors the home-screen widget, so its numbers stay close to the
      widget's own rather than being scaled up for the app.
    -->
    <!--
      Battery card. Mirrors the home-screen widget, so its numbers stay close to the
      widget's own rather than being scaled up for the app.
    -->
    <dimen name="battery_card_padding">14dp</dimen>
    <!--
      Vertical padding spends height WITHOUT inflating any child. The user asked for
      a visibly bigger box three times and the previous 18dp was not enough, so this
      is now 24dp — the card grows by ~48dp of padding alone, which is the difference
      that makes the box read as deliberately large rather than as a tight strip.
    -->
    <dimen name="battery_card_padding_v">24dp</dimen>

    <!--
      ICON SIZES — aligned so the buds and the case share a common centre line.

      THE ALIGNMENT PROBLEM: the buds are portrait and the case is landscape. With a
      40dp square bud and a 40x32 case, the two have different vertical centres once
      the row centres them, so the case sat visibly high or low against the buds.

      The fix is to give them a COMMON HEIGHT and let each fill its own width:
          bud   40 x 40   (portrait, fills its square)
          case  48 x 40   (landscape, fills its wider slot)
      Both are 40dp tall, so `gravity="center_vertical"` on the row aligns them
      exactly, and the case's greater width no longer implies a different height.
      This is also what stops the case being clipped: its slot is now the full 40dp
      tall, which is what the drawable's intrinsic size expects.
    -->
    <!--
      THE WEAR ICONS — three separate drawables, copied verbatim from local/svgs/.

          ic_bud_left.xml   176 x 272  (local/svgs/left.svg)
          ic_case.xml       496 x 400  (local/svgs/case.svg)
          ic_bud_right.xml  176 x 272  (local/svgs/right.svg)

      The buds are tall, the case is wide, so the three CANNOT share one box. They
      share a HEIGHT: `battery_wear_height` is the common height, and each icon is
      given an EXPLICIT width computed from its own ratio.

      WHY THE WIDTHS ARE EXPLICIT AND NOT `wrap_content + adjustViewBounds`:
      that combination clips the artwork. The drawable's intrinsic size is stored in
      PIXELS at the screen density, so declaring 24dp x 37dp becomes 63 x 97 px at
      2.625 (37 * 2.625 = 97.125, rounded DOWN to 97). The resulting intrinsic ratio,
      63:97 = 0.649, no longer matches the SVG's true ratio. adjustViewBounds
      then sizes the view from the DISTORTED ratio (62.1dp wide at 96dp tall) while
      the vector rasterises at the true ratio, and the difference shows up as the
      artwork being clipped at the box's bounds.

      Sizing the box explicitly from the TRUE ratio removes the mismatch. The values
      below are the source ratios applied to `battery_wear_height`:

          bud   0.647 x 96 = 62.1 -> 62dp
          case  1.240 x 96 = 119.0 -> 119dp

      Change `battery_wear_height` and scale these three widths with it (the case
      width is 1.240/0.647 = 1.917x the bud width).
    -->
    <dimen name="battery_wear_height">96dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="battery_bud_width">62dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="battery_case_width">119dp</dimen>
    <!--
      Gap between the icons. The SVGs' ink runs to their viewBox edges, so with no
      margin the three read as one touching mass; this separates them. Applied as the
      case's start and end margin, which spaces bud : case : bud at once.
      
      Total icon block width = 62 + 10 + 124 + 10 + 62 = 268dp, inside the card's
      351dp inner width, so the block still centres with room either side.
    -->
    <dimen name="battery_icon_gap">10dp</dimen>

    <!--
      WIDGET bud column.

      `widget_bud_width` and `widget_bud_height` are a MATCHED PAIR: the box must
      carry the artwork's TRUE ratio (0.641) or `fitCenter` stretches the ink to the
      box's shape. Two bugs came from breaking that rule:

        1. 34dp wide x ~74dp tall box -> ink rendered 34 x 53dp: SQUISHED
           horizontally with dead space above and below, because the width was the
           binding constraint.
        2. 72dp wide x ~70dp tall box -> ink rendered 72 x 96dp, a ratio of 0.75
           against the true 0.641: FAT on the vertical axis, exactly as reported.
           The box was wider than the ratio needs, so the art scaled UP in width.

      So: 72 / 0.641 = 112dp. Height 112dp against width 72dp reproduces the source
      viewBox (460 x 717.456) at 0.641 and the ink can no longer be distorted.

      SIZED TO FIT A 2x2 WIDGET. At 2x2 the widget is ~130dp wide, leaving roughly
      ~108dp of card width; a 72dp bud plus 8dp gap plus 72dp bud = 152dp does NOT
      fit, which is why the left bud was CUT OFF at 2x2 while looking fine at 3x2.
      The pair is therefore 48 x 75dp (48 / 0.641 = 74.9), giving 48 + 8 + 48 =
      104dp, which fits the 2x2 card with a little room and still grows on larger
      widgets because the row height stretches.

      CHANGE THESE TWO TOGETHER, ALWAYS AT RATIO 0.641, or the buds distort again.
      The in-app battery card uses the same rule (battery_bud_width 62dp /
      battery_wear_height 96dp = 0.646) — match that pattern.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_bud_width">48dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="widget_bud_height">75dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="widget_bud_gap">8dp</dimen>
    <!-- Kept for the drawables' own logical size; not used for layout sizing. -->
    <dimen name="battery_bud_size">96dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="battery_case_height">96dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="battery_letter_size">20dp</dimen>

    <!--
      Battery bar height. Raised so the 10 segment dividers stay legible and the
      in-bar number has room: at 10dp the dividers were crowding the digits, which
      was reported as "the text is hard to read". 13dp gives the numerals real
      clearance.
    -->
    <dimen name="battery_bar_height">13dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="battery_row_spacing">9dp</dimen>

    <!--
      Circular ANC buttons. Diameter is driven by the four needing to fit across
      a 5" screen with margins: 4 x 62dp + 3 x 12dp gaps = 284dp, which leaves
      room inside the 16dp screen padding on a 320dp-wide screen.
    -->
    <dimen name="anc_circle_size">62dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="anc_circle_gap">12dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="anc_circle_ring">2dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="anc_circle_text_size">11sp</dimen>
    <!--
      ANC buttons are rounded RECTANGLES now, not circles, and stretch to fill the
      row so there is no empty space at the left and right edges. Height is
      independent of the old diameter; the width is driven by weight.
    -->
    <dimen name="anc_button_height">52dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="anc_button_radius">14dp</dimen>

    <!-- Settings rows: label left, control right. -->
    <dimen name="setting_row_height">56dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="setting_row_padding_horizontal">14dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="setting_label_size">15sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="setting_sub_label_size">12sp</dimen>

    <!-- Switch track / thumb. Sized here because the switch is tinted in code. -->
    <dimen name="setting_switch_width">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="setting_switch_height">26dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="setting_switch_thumb">22dp</dimen>

    <!-- Chevron button at the right of a row that opens another screen. -->
    <dimen name="setting_chevron_size">32dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="setting_icon_size">22dp</dimen>

    <!-- Card corner radius, matching widget_card_bg's 16dp. -->
    <dimen name="app_card_radius">16dp</dimen>
</resources>
